> THE PARCEL <

# Act One

FADE IN:

INT. KITCHEN MORNING

Sunlight slants across the tiled floor. JANE pours coffee, watching the steam curl up.

@ [[JANE]]
I should have stayed in bed.

EST. STREET

A delivery truck idles. The driver checks his clipboard.

= Synopsis: Jane begins her day, unaware that the parcel will change everything.

EXT. FRONT DOOR DAY

The truck door slams. Footsteps on gravel. A doorbell.

@ JANE
Already?

CUT TO:

I/E. CAR DUSK

The interior is dim. Jane drives one-handed, the parcel on the passenger seat.

! NOTE: Jane checks the mirror but doesn't see the car behind her.

@ JANE
Just a few more miles.
The parcel pulses on the seat.
Something inside it knows.

DISSOLVE TO:

# Act Two

EXT. WAREHOUSE NIGHT

A single bulb above a steel door. Jane approaches, parcel held tight.

She *carefully* unwraps the corner of the parcel. Inside: a key, **gleaming** in the dim light. A tag reads _do not open_.

. MIRROR POV

The reflection holds a beat too long. Jane doesn't notice. The parcel sees ***everything***.

/* The original ending dropped here was too dark for the test screening; reinstate if the studio asks. */

SMASH CUT TO:

EXT. WAREHOUSE NIGHT

Empty. Jane is gone. The parcel sits on the doorstep.

FADE OUT.

> THE END <

